ifa/issues/118 -- {bool, None} has no representation without boxing: bool is 1 byte, None is pointer-sized, and determine_layouts refuses the mixed-width slot ("mismatched field sizes: class 'closure' field '<anon>' mixes 1- and 8-byte members"). Reduced from chess, whose rowAttack has exactly this shape. {None, int64} already works by bit-for-bit round-trip, so this fails only on WIDTH -- but widening the FA-side layout is measured insufficient (PYC_WIDEN_UNION_FIELD gets past the check and into 18 C errors, because the member's declared C type comes out `void`). CPython prints False, which the check file records, so this flips to PASS when a representation for mixed-width unions lands.
